[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Cut-specific cooking for [b]Build 42[/b]. Every cut of meat has a best way to cook it and a best doneness, the dish is named after how you made it, and a meal cooked right lifts your mood. A Cooking window lays out every dish, pot and stove within reach. Works with vanilla meat on its own, and with every Dazed Butchery cut and grade.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes, dedicated servers included[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Works with[/b][/td][td]Dazed Butchery, Dazed Climate (both optional)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedCooking[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-cut.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/doneness.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/cuts.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Raw cuts say what they want in the tooltip, e.g. “Best: Grilled / Pan-seared, Medium rare – Medium”.
[*]Cook it in a stove or oven, on a barbecue, campfire or fireplace, or in a smoker. The method comes from where it cooked.
[*]Once it counts as cooked, the tooltip shows doneness live: Rare, Medium rare, Medium, Well done, Burnt.
[*]Take it out at the right moment. The dish is named for it: “Grilled Ribeye Steak (Choice, Medium rare)”.
[*]Eight kinds of cut, each with its own best method and doneness: steak, roast, slow, ribs, chop, pork roast, poultry and offal.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-mood.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/mood.png[/img]
[list]
[*]A cut cooked the right way to the right doneness lifts your mood and eases boredom and stress.
[*]Dazed Butchery's grade multiplies it: a Prime cut done right is the best meal you can have.
[*]A microwaved or burnt cut leaves you a little unhappy.
[*]With [b]Dazed Climate[/b], hot food eaten somewhere colder than 12 °C warms you for up to an hour, and a hot drink for up to half an hour.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-portion.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/portion.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click a raw primal with a knife to cut it into portions: a Beef Rib becomes three Ribeye Steaks, a Pork Loin four Loin Chops, a Venison Backstrap four Medallions.
[*]Portions keep the primal's food, age and grade.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-window.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/window.png[/img]
Right-click a pot, pan, bowl or bread, or a stove, oven, grill or fire, and pick [b]Open Cooking Window[/b]. You can also bind a key in the Mods options.
[list]
[*][b]Cook[/b]: pick a dish (stew, soup, stir fry, salad, sandwich, pie, pasta and the rest of the game's own) and a pot or pan in reach. The grid shows every ingredient nearby the dish takes, with Butchery grade letters. [b]Add to pot[/b], see what the pot will make with its hunger and calories, then [b]Put on Stove[/b].
[*][b]On the Heat[/b]: every stove, oven, microwave, barbecue, fireplace and campfire within 12 tiles on your floor, with a doneness bar for cuts and a cooking bar for pots. [b]Take Off[/b] moves it to your inventory. An optional note warns you shortly before something burns.
[*][b]Recipes[/b]: save a pot as a named recipe, see what you have, what is missing and what can stand in, then [b]Cook Again[/b]. Your recipe book is kept on your computer, so it follows you between saves.
[*][b]Quick add[/b]: right-click a pot, [b]Add Ingredient[/b], pick the dish and use the + buttons.
[/list]
Every change goes through the game's own actions, so the window is multiplayer safe. It does nothing while closed.

The in-game [b]Dazed Mod Suite Guide[/b] from Dazed Core has a Cooking tab.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-sandbox.png[/img]
Good Food Mood Bonus (0 turns it off), Named Dishes, Cooking Tips in Tooltips and Hot Food Warms You. The burn warning and the window's key are player options on the Dazed page of the Mods options.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Vanilla meat works without Dazed Butchery; Butchery adds its cuts, grades and portioning.
[*]Hot food warmth needs [b]Dazed Climate[/b]. Without it nothing changes.
[*]Builds on the game's own cooking, evolved recipes and timed actions. The window can't take an ingredient back out of a pot, because the game can't either.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

